===Etymology===
Named after the [[Cayuse]] tribe of the Pacific Northwest. However, the etymology of this tribe name is unknown; it may be an exonym, and may in fact come from Spanish {{m|es|caballo|t=horse}}, which is the source of the word for horse in many Native American languages of western North America.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkaɪuːs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|US}} A small [[Indian]] [[horse]] or [[pony]].

